# Required: local CosyVoice. Mac steps (download ~2 GB, where to put it,
# prompt wav, cpu vs mps vs Intel): docs/cosyvoice.md
# Weights stay outside git. CPU works and is slow (seconds per sentence).
# On a Mac start with cpu. mps is Apple Silicon only and best-effort.
# cuda is NVIDIA, not a Mac.
COSYVOICE_REPO=/Users/you/src/CosyVoice
COSYVOICE_MODEL_DIR=/Users/you/models/CosyVoice2-0.5B
COSYVOICE_PROMPT_WAV=/Users/you/models/jarvis-prompt.wav
COSYVOICE_PROMPT_TEXT=The words spoken in prompt.wav.
COSYVOICE_DEVICE=cpu
# COSYVOICE_SPEAKER=jarvis
# COSYVOICE_TIMEOUT=120

# Unused. Speech does not read this. Not shown in Settings.
# FISH_API_KEY=your-fish-audio-api-key-here

# Cursor CLI. The voice brain and every construction run spawn `agent`
# (or `cursor-agent`) and use the login you already have from `agent login`.
# No API key is read or required. If the binary is not on PATH, point at it:
# JARVIS_CURSOR_AGENT=/usr/local/bin/agent

# Optional: model passed as `--model` to the Cursor CLI.
# JARVIS_BRAIN_MODEL=sonnet
# JARVIS_RUN_MODEL=sonnet

# Unused. Not shown in Settings.
# FISH_VOICE_ID=your-fish-voice-id-here

# Optional: Your name (JARVIS will address you by name)
# USER_NAME=Tony

# Optional: pass `--force` to construction runs so the Cursor CLI does not
# stop on a permission prompt. Defaults to true because JARVIS is
# voice-driven and cannot answer those prompts (they would hang the run).
# Set to "false" only when you can answer prompts in a terminal you can see.
# JARVIS_SKIP_PERMISSIONS=true

# Optional: Override the auto-detected weather location.
# By default, JARVIS uses your public-IP location (via ipwho.is) and reports
# Fahrenheit. Set these to pin a specific location:
# WEATHER_LOCATION_LABEL=London
# WEATHER_LATITUDE=51.5072
# WEATHER_LONGITUDE=-0.1276
# WEATHER_UNIT=fahrenheit  # or "celsius"
